CAT = "rsttmCommon"; SEG = "COM"
Q = [
("Before working under a raised cab-over cab, what keeps it from coming down?",
 "The mechanical cab lock", ["Pressure held in the tilt pump", "A floor jack under the bumper", "The tilt cylinder's check valve"],
 "A tilted cab must rest on its mechanical lock or safety stop, not on hydraulic pressure. A pump valve or check valve that leaks can let the cab drop."),
("Which step comes first before arc welding on a truck frame with electronic modules?",
 "Disconnect the batteries", ["Ground the welder on the axle", "Leave the ignition key on", "Pull the ECM fuse only"],
 "Welding current can travel through module wiring. Disconnect the batteries (and modules where the OEM says so) and clamp the ground close to the weld on the same part."),
("A hybrid truck's high-voltage system must be serviced. What protects the technician's hands?",
 "Insulating gloves with protectors", ["Nitrile gloves under cotton liners", "Leather welding gauntlets", "Two pairs of mechanic's gloves"],
 "High-voltage work calls for rubber insulating gloves rated for the system voltage, inspected before use and worn under leather protectors. Ordinary work gloves do not insulate."),
("When lifting an engine out of a chassis with a shop crane, where should the hook sit?",
 "Over the centre of gravity", ["At the front lifting eye only", "As far back as the boom reaches", "Over the flywheel housing"],
 "Rigging over the centre of gravity keeps the load level and stops it from swinging or tipping off the sling. Use the lifting brackets and a spreader bar or load leveller."),
("Why are torque-to-yield head bolts not reused after removal?",
 "They are permanently stretched", ["Their threads are coated with nickel", "Their heads are too soft for sockets", "Their thread pitch changes with heat"],
 "Torque-to-yield bolts are tightened into their yield range, so they stretch for good. Reused, they can neck down or break and lose clamping force."),
("A hydraulic hose is replaced on a dump hoist. What must the new hose match?",
 "Pressure rating and end fittings", ["Cover colour and length rounded up", "Inside diameter only", "Outside diameter and bend radius"],
 "A replacement hose must meet the system's working pressure and use matching end fittings and crimp specs. A lower rating can burst under load."),
("Used engine oil and coolant are drained during a service. How are they handled?",
 "Kept apart for recycling", ["Mixed in one waste drum", "Filtered and reused in the truck", "Left in the drain pan until full"],
 "Waste fluids go into separate labelled containers and are recycled under jurisdictional rules. Mixed waste can no longer be recycled."),
("A wheel bearing is packed with grease. Which grease should be used?",
 "The type the OEM specifies", ["Any grease of the same colour", "Chassis grease with moly", "The heaviest grade on the shelf"],
 "Greases differ in base oil, thickener and temperature range, and some are incompatible when mixed. Follow the manufacturer's specification for the hub."),
("A new lip seal is installed on a hub. Which way does the lip face?",
 "Toward the lubricant", ["Toward the outside air", "Toward the brake drum", "Either way if greased"],
 "The sealing lip points at the oil or grease so pressure presses it against the shaft. Installed backwards, the seal leaks once the cavity fills."),
("A technician finds a fault code that the repair manual does not list. What is the next step?",
 "Look for an OEM bulletin", ["Clear it and return the truck", "Replace the module that set it", "Disregard it if the truck runs"],
 "Service bulletins and updated OEM information cover codes and fixes added after the manual was printed. Clearing codes or swapping modules without a diagnosis wastes time."),
("Which record is completed when a repair is finished?",
 "Completed work order", ["A sticky note on the dash", "The parts invoice alone", "The driver's trip log"],
 "The work order records the complaint, cause and correction, parts used and test results. Fleets and warranty claims rely on it, and it helps the next diagnosis."),
("An apprentice is learning to set slack adjusters. What helps the skill stick?",
 "Supervised hands-on practice", ["Reading the manual alone", "Watching you do every one", "A short talk over lunch"],
 "Mentoring works best when the learner practises the task with feedback right away. Demonstrate, let them do it, then check the result together."),
]
